{
  "kind": "completeness_consistency_v1",
  "description": "RFC 6962 section 2.1.2 consistency proofs for the completeness receipt tree (build1-completeness-witnessing, P5). A consistency proof between tree sizes m < n proves tree(m) is a leaf-prefix of tree(n): the first m leaves are unchanged, unreordered, unremoved, and growth was append-only at the tail. Verification is the RFC 9162 section 2.1.4.2 iterative algorithm. Two independent anchors: (1) the canonical RFC 6962 reference 8-leaf tree with raw-byte leaves and its published roots and proofs, proving byte-for-byte agreement with sigstore Rekor / Trillian; (2) SynOI completeness cases whose leaves follow ADR_023 D1 (leafHash of the 64-char hex OID STRING), covering a valid append-only extension (accept) and rewritten/reordered/mutated/truncated histories (reject). All hashes are bare lowercase hex. A reimplementation in any language reproduces every value from the ordered inputs alone. HONESTY BOUNDARY: a consistency proof establishes ONLY the append-only structural relation between two roots; it does not prove the leaves are complete or honest, does not catch back-dating into the still-unwitnessed tail (indices m..n), and does not anchor either root to a public log.",
  "constants": {
    "algorithm": "RFC6962-SHA256",
    "leaf_raw_bytes": "RFC KAT block: leafHash(data) = SHA-256(0x00 || data) over raw bytes",
    "leaf_hex_string": "SynOI block: leafHash(oid_hex) = SHA-256(0x00 || utf8(oid_hex_64)) per ADR_023 D1 (leaf hashes the hex STRING, not the raw 32 digest bytes)",
    "internal_node": "internalHash(l,r) = SHA-256(0x01 || l || r)",
    "proof_wire_form": "ordered array of 64-hex node hashes, NO L/R tags; structure derived from (m,n) arithmetic at verify time (RFC 6962 wire form, Rekor/Trillian compatible)",
    "verify_algorithm": "RFC 9162 section 2.1.4.2 VerifyConsistency; m===0 -> empty proof accepts; 0<m<n -> non-empty proof required; when m is a power of two the prior root is omitted and verification seeds from the supplied prior root; both prior and current roots must reconstruct exactly and no proof nodes may be left unconsumed"
